    "changelog_excerpt": "# 🚀 DMTools Release v1.7.288\n\n## 📝 What's Changed\n\nFull diff: [v1.7.287...v1.7.288](https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/compare/v1.7.287...v1.7.288)\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- Add MCP initialize session handshake and guard installer against stale manifest (#823, #829) (#832) (0b2c442e)\n- Never write .cursor/skills into workspace in global skill installs (IstiN/dmtools-agents#1397) (#845) (5bffe630)\n- Preserve <br/> line breaks in storage bodies and table cells (#827) (#828) (16f0481e)\n\n### 📦 Dependencies\n- Auth (#842) (bc967532)\n- Bump actions/setup-java from 6.1.0 to 6.2.0 (#835) (f7bab801)\n- Bump katex and mermaid in /landing (#836) (67ef2d47)\n- Bump versions.graalvm from 25.4.4.1.1 to 25.5.5.0.3 (#837) (53863a36)\n- Google-auth-library-oauth2-http (#840) (0aae1894)\n- Google-cloud-core (#839) (dc2fa3a7)\n- Jsoup from 1.23.2 to 1.24.1 (#843) (33e7d860)\n- Regions (#844) (aec7671e)\n\n### 🛠 Maintenance\n- Update coverage badge (#830) (534f013a)\n- Update coverage badge (#833) (d5a273aa)\n- Update site data for v1.7.287 (#831) (243d86ec)\n\n---\n\nThis release includes the **DMTools CLI** and **Agent Skill** for enterprise dark-factory orchestration across MCP tools, AI agents, and delivery workflows.\n\n## 📦 What's Included\n\n### 🖥️ DMTools CLI\n- **Command-line interface** for DMTools operations\n- **Java-based** automation and integration tools\n- **Cross-platform install scripts** for easy setup (`install`, `install.sh`, `install.bat`, `install.ps1`)\n- **Wrapper script** (`dmtools.sh`)\n\n### 🤖 DMTools Agent Skill\n- **AI assistant skill** for MCP, AI agents, and generative-ai-friendly DMTools workflows in Cursor, Claude, Codex, and other Agent Skills compatible systems\n- **Complete DMtools documentation** (67+ MCP tools, JavaScript agent development, and configuration guides)\n- **Cross-platform support** (works with all major AI coding assistants)\n\n## 🎯 Quick Start\n\n### Install DMTools CLI\n\n**macOS / Linux / Git Bash:**\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/epam/dm.ai/releases/latest/download/..."
